  "Question": "The sum of two numbers is 20, and their difference is 6. Find the two numbers. (Write the larger number first, followed by the smaller number, separated by a comma.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "13，7",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Let the larger number be \\(x\\) and the smaller number be \\(y\\): \\(x+y=20\\), \\(x-y=6\\). Adding gives \\(2x=26\\), so \\(x=13\\), \\(y=7\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Equalize the numbers\n\nSubtracting \\(6\\) from the larger number makes it equal to the smaller number. Their total is now \\(20-6\\), made up of two copies of the smaller number. Thus the smaller number is\n\\[\n(20-6)\\div2=7.\n\\]\nAdding back the difference gives the larger number, \\(7+6=13\\). The answer is \\(13,7\\).",
